1
00:00:03,509 --> 00:00:05,886
[LESTRADE] The first
victim was a prostitute,

2
00:00:05,928 --> 00:00:07,554
last seen with a john.

3
00:00:07,596 --> 00:00:09,014
He's been described as blond,

4
00:00:09,055 --> 00:00:13,185
fair-skinned, and standing
about six feet tall.

5
00:00:13,226 --> 00:00:16,981
When the body was found,
she was barely recognisable.

6
00:00:17,022 --> 00:00:18,273
Her throat was slit.

7
00:00:18,315 --> 00:00:22,820
And her internal organs had
been meticulously removed.

8
00:00:22,862 --> 00:00:26,114
Then, a week later,
another prostitute was seen

9
00:00:26,156 --> 00:00:28,450
with a man who had
a swarthy complexion.

10
00:00:28,492 --> 00:00:31,036
Additionally, this
individual was shorter than

11
00:00:31,077 --> 00:00:34,874
the first suspect at
five and a half feet tall.

12
00:00:34,915 --> 00:00:36,333
Immediately afterward,

13
00:00:36,375 --> 00:00:39,461
she was killed in
an identical manner.

14
00:00:39,503 --> 00:00:41,380
Based on the eyewitness reports,

15
00:00:41,421 --> 00:00:45,342
we surmised that one of the two
men is the Whitechapel killer.

16
00:00:45,384 --> 00:00:48,345
Then our investigation
took a twist.

17
00:00:48,387 --> 00:00:50,514
A man calling himself
"Jack the Ripper"

18
00:00:50,556 --> 00:00:54,059
stepped forth, claiming
credit for both murders.

19
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:56,269
[HOLMES]
Just one question.

20
00:00:56,311 --> 00:00:58,814
You built all of
this for me, Lestrade?

21
00:00:58,856 --> 00:01:00,900
[LESTRADE]
Naturally. Nothing worse than

22
00:01:00,941 --> 00:01:03,443
an unengaging presenter.

23
00:01:03,485 --> 00:01:07,072
I'll ask once again.
Help me catch this vile criminal

24
00:01:07,113 --> 00:01:10,034
before he adds more
to his grim tally.

25
00:01:10,075 --> 00:01:13,620
[LESTRADE]
Holmes, please!

26
00:01:13,662 --> 00:01:14,496
I'll pass.

27
00:01:14,538 --> 00:01:15,873
[WATSON grunts]

28
00:02:47,131 --> 00:02:49,842
[JACK] Young Will,
you already have suspicions

29
00:02:49,883 --> 00:02:52,136
regarding the
identity of the culprit?

30
00:02:52,177 --> 00:02:56,222
Yes, the real killer
is actually a group.

31
00:02:56,264 --> 00:02:58,558
Organized crime to be specific.

32
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:00,102
[GROUP grunts]

33
00:03:00,144 --> 00:03:02,437
You're basing that
on what exactly?

34
00:03:02,479 --> 00:03:05,024
[WILLIAM] First of all,
ask yourself why the killers

35
00:03:05,065 --> 00:03:06,650
would claim to be
Jack the Ripper

36
00:03:06,692 --> 00:03:09,486
and write to the newspapers.

37
00:03:09,528 --> 00:03:11,780
It's simple.
Their objective is to

38
00:03:11,822 --> 00:03:14,574
have a platform for
their criminal acts.

39
00:03:14,616 --> 00:03:19,705
In short, a means of stirring
up fear among the citizens.

40
00:03:19,746 --> 00:03:22,499
As for adopting the
maestro's old nickname,

41
00:03:22,541 --> 00:03:25,002
it was likely an
odd coincidence.

42
00:03:25,044 --> 00:03:26,920
Any name would
have been sufficient,

43
00:03:26,962 --> 00:03:29,756
so long as it stoked dread.

44
00:03:29,798 --> 00:03:32,134
Thus, it's presumable
killing the prostitutes

45
00:03:32,176 --> 00:03:34,594
wasn't their goal
but simply a means to

46
00:03:34,636 --> 00:03:37,181
furthering their ultimate plan.

47
00:03:37,222 --> 00:03:39,892
These killings were
done for dramatic effect.

48
00:03:39,933 --> 00:03:41,351
As we've established,

49
00:03:41,393 --> 00:03:43,854
fanning the flames of
terror was the first step,

50
00:03:43,896 --> 00:03:46,606
but there was also
another objective at play.

51
00:03:46,648 --> 00:03:49,068
And what objective is that?

52
00:03:49,109 --> 00:03:50,485
Revolt.

53
00:03:50,527 --> 00:03:52,154
To incite a battle between

54
00:03:52,196 --> 00:03:54,489
the town's Vigilance
Committee and the Yard.

55
00:03:54,531 --> 00:03:57,701
Once the two sides begin
to clash, it'll escalate.

56
00:03:57,743 --> 00:04:01,705
Setting off a proletarian
revolution within Britain.

57
00:04:01,747 --> 00:04:04,583
[SOLDIERS yell]

58
00:04:04,624 --> 00:04:07,961
Indeed. Such an act is
an enormous undertaking.

59
00:04:08,003 --> 00:04:10,630
The difficulty of one
person carrying it out

60
00:04:10,672 --> 00:04:13,092
would be unimaginable.

61
00:04:13,133 --> 00:04:15,135
[WILLIAM] These culprits,
they've fashioned

62
00:04:15,177 --> 00:04:17,804
a fictional devil and
called him "Jack the Ripper."

63
00:04:17,846 --> 00:04:19,723
Setting the stage for
the Vigilance Committee

64
00:04:19,765 --> 00:04:21,266
to take up arms.

65
00:04:21,307 --> 00:04:24,644
If another murder occurs,
the results will be disastrous.

66
00:04:24,686 --> 00:04:26,646
Conflict between the
Yard and the citizenry

67
00:04:26,688 --> 00:04:27,814
will be unavoidable

68
00:04:27,856 --> 00:04:30,817
and will serve as the
catalyst for an uprising.

69
00:04:30,859 --> 00:04:34,320
If that's true, we have a
problem. Since they're a group,

70
00:04:34,362 --> 00:04:37,157
it'll be hard rounding them up
at the same time and place.

71
00:04:37,199 --> 00:04:39,118
[WILLIAM]
Not to worry.

72
00:04:39,159 --> 00:04:44,039
It'll be a test for the
Moriarty Plan... our goal.

73
00:04:44,081 --> 00:04:45,665
Hm.

74
00:04:56,927 --> 00:04:59,221
[GUARD 16A]
Hm? Huh?

75
00:05:00,931 --> 00:05:03,016
[CIVILIAN 16A growls]

76
00:05:03,058 --> 00:05:04,810
[GUARD 16A growls]

77
00:05:13,277 --> 00:05:15,112
[GUARD 16A]
Hm.

78
00:05:15,154 --> 00:05:17,823
[yelping]

79
00:05:20,659 --> 00:05:23,078
Whew, it's just
a cat, that's all.

80
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:24,579
Huh?

81
00:05:24,621 --> 00:05:26,581
[gasps]

82
00:05:26,623 --> 00:05:28,458
[whistle sounds]

83
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:29,918
[CIVILIANS panting]

84
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:31,962
[POLICE panting]

85
00:05:34,506 --> 00:05:36,925
You expect us to let
the Yard handle this case?

86
00:05:36,967 --> 00:05:39,136
This is our town, and
we'll protect it ourselves!

87
00:05:39,178 --> 00:05:40,679
[POLICE gasp]

88
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:41,930
[POLICE growl]

89
00:05:41,972 --> 00:05:45,809
[CROWD growls]

90
00:05:48,895 --> 00:05:50,022
[WOMAN 16A screams]

91
00:05:50,063 --> 00:05:50,981
What's that?!

92
00:05:51,023 --> 00:05:52,565
[POLICE gasp]

93
00:05:54,943 --> 00:05:56,611
[chuckles]

94
00:05:59,990 --> 00:06:00,782
- -[CROWD gasps]

95
00:06:00,824 --> 00:06:03,785
- -[JACK cackles]
- -[CROWD gasps]

96
00:06:03,827 --> 00:06:06,371
[JACK] My presence
stills the crying child!

97
00:06:06,412 --> 00:06:08,165
I'm Jack the Ripper!

98
00:06:08,207 --> 00:06:10,292
I've witnessed
the strangest things

99
00:06:10,334 --> 00:06:12,252
from the rooftops and alleys.

100
00:06:12,294 --> 00:06:14,254
War is brewing in Whitechapel.

101
00:06:14,296 --> 00:06:17,590
I certainly hope you didn't
expect me to sit it out.

102
00:06:17,632 --> 00:06:19,801
- -[CROWD gasps]
- -[JACK] By all means, proceed.

103
00:06:19,843 --> 00:06:21,261
While you fight one another,

104
00:06:21,303 --> 00:06:23,596
I can kill to
my heart's content!

105
00:06:23,638 --> 00:06:32,022
[JACK cackling]

106
00:06:32,064 --> 00:06:32,647
[JACK grunts]

107
00:06:32,689 --> 00:06:34,566
[CROWD gasps]

108
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:39,404
[JACK] What's wrong? No bother
in letting me run free?

109
00:06:39,445 --> 00:06:41,948
[CROWD gasps]

110
00:06:41,990 --> 00:06:44,784
- -[CIVILIAN 16E grunts]
- -[CROWD shouts]

111
00:06:47,954 --> 00:06:50,707
[POLICEMAN 16B] After him, lads!
We can't let him escape!

112
00:06:50,749 --> 00:06:52,209
Goes for us, too!

113
00:06:52,251 --> 00:06:53,626
[CIVILIANS]
Yeah!

114
00:06:56,088 --> 00:06:57,339
[MORAN]
So that's it.

115
00:06:57,381 --> 00:07:00,466
The old man's playing the
common enemy to both sides,

116
00:07:00,508 --> 00:07:02,594
unifying the Yard and
the Vigilance Committee,

117
00:07:02,635 --> 00:07:04,429
not dividing them.

118
00:07:04,470 --> 00:07:06,181
Yes.

119
00:07:06,223 --> 00:07:07,640
A favour, Fred.

120
00:07:07,682 --> 00:07:10,894
Go to the morgue and procure
three autopsied corpses.

121
00:07:10,936 --> 00:07:12,229
Consider it done.

122
00:07:12,271 --> 00:07:15,399
I'll prepare some stage
blood for the performance, too.

123
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:16,858
[WILLIAM]
Moran and Bonde,

124
00:07:16,900 --> 00:07:18,944
I need you to pick up
some weapons from Herder.

125
00:07:18,985 --> 00:07:20,570
Who is this Herder?

126
00:07:20,612 --> 00:07:22,114
A friend of ours
with probably the

127
00:07:22,155 --> 00:07:24,490
biggest weapon
stockpile in all London.

128
00:07:24,532 --> 00:07:27,244
Once the actual Jack the Ripper
shows up in the flesh,

129
00:07:27,286 --> 00:07:29,329
the criminals are sure to
gather together so as to

130
00:07:29,371 --> 00:07:31,373
plan out their next
move in response.

131
00:07:31,415 --> 00:07:32,874
That's when we'll strike.

132
00:07:32,916 --> 00:07:33,833
But how are we going to

133
00:07:33,875 --> 00:07:36,295
uncover the location
of the rendezvous?

134
00:07:36,336 --> 00:07:38,546
[WILLIAM] That's where
Albert enters the equation.

135
00:07:38,588 --> 00:07:41,841
We'll consult military
intelligence for answers.

136
00:07:41,883 --> 00:07:45,762
Maestro, until we can confirm
the location of their assembly,

137
00:07:45,804 --> 00:07:47,847
I'll need you
to buy us some time.

138
00:07:47,889 --> 00:07:51,851
Happy to. A game of tag,
or rather hide and seek.

139
00:07:51,893 --> 00:07:53,519
[MORAN]
No offense to the old man,

140
00:07:53,561 --> 00:07:55,563
but between the Yard
and Vigilance Committee,

141
00:07:55,605 --> 00:07:58,733
we're talking 300 men,
and if he can't kill anyone--

142
00:07:58,775 --> 00:08:00,068
Absolutely no killing

143
00:08:00,110 --> 00:08:02,904
and I'd like you to refrain
from harming anyone as well.

144
00:08:02,946 --> 00:08:04,697
That's a pretty tall
order you know.

145
00:08:04,739 --> 00:08:06,783
I'm not sure I could
last for ten minutes.

146
00:08:06,825 --> 00:08:09,328
Well, I reckon I could
run for half an hour.

147
00:08:09,369 --> 00:08:10,203
[MORAN]
Hm?

148
00:08:10,245 --> 00:08:13,039
[WILLIAM]
Two hours... if you can.

149
00:08:13,081 --> 00:08:16,376
But I need you to hold out for
one hour at the very minimum.

150
00:08:16,918 --> 00:08:18,753
[POLICEMAN 16C]
There he goes!

151
00:08:18,795 --> 00:08:20,130
[CIVILIAN 16E]
Hold it right there, you rotter!

152
00:08:20,172 --> 00:08:22,424
[JACK panting]

153
00:08:22,466 --> 00:08:25,802
[POLICEMAN 16D grunting]

154
00:08:25,844 --> 00:08:27,553
[POLICEMAN 16D groans]

155
00:08:27,595 --> 00:08:28,388
[POLICEMAN 16D groans]

156
00:08:28,430 --> 00:08:29,514
[JACK]
Young Will,

157
00:08:29,555 --> 00:08:32,476
this plan you concocted
is positively insane.

158
00:08:32,517 --> 00:08:33,143
[JACK grunts]

159
00:08:33,185 --> 00:08:34,102
[CIVILIAN 16D]
Take aim!

160
00:08:34,144 --> 00:08:35,354
[JACK gasps]

161
00:08:37,689 --> 00:08:38,857
[JACK chuckles]

162
00:08:38,898 --> 00:08:40,233
His cloak deflected it!

163
00:08:40,275 --> 00:08:43,111
Is it armoured? Stop him!

164
00:08:43,153 --> 00:08:45,071
[JACK] Even though the
weight is a slight drawback,

165
00:08:45,113 --> 00:08:46,239
I can't complain.

166
00:08:46,281 --> 00:08:48,533
At least it's not hindering
me from my mission.

167
00:08:48,574 --> 00:08:49,993
One, keep running.

168
00:08:50,035 --> 00:08:51,495
Second of all, no killing.

169
00:08:51,536 --> 00:08:53,497
And third, don't get captured.

170
00:08:53,538 --> 00:08:54,747
My role is to do nothing

171
00:08:54,789 --> 00:08:57,750
but buy time until all our
enemies are in one place.

172
00:08:57,792 --> 00:08:59,836
There he is! I've got him!

173
00:09:02,797 --> 00:09:04,257
[CIVILIAN 16F yelps]
What?

174
00:09:04,299 --> 00:09:07,302
How did that happen?
My gun went off by itself!

175
00:09:07,344 --> 00:09:14,559
[POLICEMAN 16E]
Give me that! I'll do it!

176
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:17,354
[JACK chuckles]
Looks like our sharpshooter's

177
00:09:17,396 --> 00:09:19,022
better than yours.

178
00:09:28,865 --> 00:09:29,991
I'm impressed you can hit them

179
00:09:30,033 --> 00:09:31,784
at this range
without a scope.

180
00:09:31,826 --> 00:09:34,787
[MORAN] What? You expected me
to use that pirate spyglass?

181
00:09:34,829 --> 00:09:36,248
Wait. More of them!

182
00:09:36,289 --> 00:09:38,417
One at two o'clock
and another at ten!

183
00:09:38,458 --> 00:09:40,668
[MORAN]
Yeah, I see them.

184
00:09:42,128 --> 00:09:43,296
We're in the clear.

185
00:09:43,338 --> 00:09:44,339
Doesn't seem like any of them

186
00:09:44,381 --> 00:09:46,925
have the faintest idea
they've been sniped.

187
00:09:46,966 --> 00:09:51,346
[HERDER chuckles] So, in
other words, a rousing success.

188
00:09:51,388 --> 00:09:52,889
Since it's an
enhanced prototype,

189
00:09:52,931 --> 00:09:54,682
my presence was
required in the field

190
00:09:54,724 --> 00:09:57,102
in case certain
disruptions were to occur.

191
00:09:57,143 --> 00:10:00,813
Fortunately, looks like my
services weren't required.

192
00:10:00,855 --> 00:10:02,399
Nah, fine gun.

193
00:10:02,441 --> 00:10:04,276
But the trajectory
tends to slice--

194
00:10:04,317 --> 00:10:05,944
nothing you can't fix, Herder.

195
00:10:05,985 --> 00:10:06,945
[HERDER]
You don't say?

196
00:10:06,986 --> 00:10:09,364
It appears some
fine-tuning is in order.

197
00:10:09,406 --> 00:10:10,990
[MORAN]
All in all, I'm impressed.

198
00:10:11,032 --> 00:10:12,617
The firing's incredibly silent.

199
00:10:12,658 --> 00:10:14,327
[HERDER]
As I designed it to be.

200
00:10:14,369 --> 00:10:16,538
Just make sure you
bring it back in one piece.

201
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:18,582
Hard to extract data
when it's broken.

202
00:10:18,623 --> 00:10:21,293
Please, that happened once.

203
00:10:21,585 --> 00:10:24,045
The old man must be
pretty worn out by now.

204
00:10:24,087 --> 00:10:25,922
Let's go and back him up.

205
00:10:25,964 --> 00:10:27,673
Right-o.

206
00:10:27,715 --> 00:10:29,759
[JACK panting]

207
00:10:29,801 --> 00:10:30,718
[POLICEMAN 16C]
Over here!

208
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:32,137
[CIVILIAN 16F]
Hold it!

209
00:10:32,178 --> 00:10:32,512
[JACK]
Huh?

210
00:10:32,554 --> 00:10:33,388
[CIVILIANS]

211
00:10:33,430 --> 00:10:34,556
[POLICE]

212
00:10:34,598 --> 00:10:37,309
Twenty people in front of me,
a mob on my tail.

213
00:10:37,350 --> 00:10:40,395
What now? The alley
looks like my only escape.

214
00:10:40,437 --> 00:10:41,354
But is it?

215
00:10:41,396 --> 00:10:43,982
[JACK] Come on, Fred!
Give me a sign!

216
00:10:44,023 --> 00:10:45,817
Which way?

217
00:10:48,570 --> 00:10:51,364
[JACK]
Straight ahead? You're sure?

218
00:10:51,406 --> 00:10:53,366
Seize him!

219
00:10:53,408 --> 00:10:56,453
[JACK] Very well, straight then!

220
00:10:57,745 --> 00:10:58,913
[JACK grunting]

221
00:10:58,955 --> 00:11:00,873
[CROWD gasps]

222
00:11:03,668 --> 00:11:06,171
[JACK groans]

223
00:11:06,212 --> 00:11:07,880
[CIVILIAN 16G]
He got past us?

224
00:11:07,922 --> 00:11:09,882
[POLICEMAN 16G]
He is a monster!

225
00:11:12,469 --> 00:11:13,845
[JACK]
Now, I see.

226
00:11:13,886 --> 00:11:17,682
If I had gone that way, they
would have beaten me senseless.

227
00:11:19,476 --> 00:11:24,063
[JACK]
Thank you, Fred. You saved me.

228
00:11:24,105 --> 00:11:25,190
[POLICEMAN 16H]
Reporting in!

229
00:11:25,231 --> 00:11:27,400
He's heading down the
street, Chief Inspector!

230
00:11:27,442 --> 00:11:30,362
Good. Roll out
the welcome wagon!

231
00:11:30,403 --> 00:11:33,698
He screws with the Yard,
we'll show him what happens.

232
00:11:37,910 --> 00:11:40,330
There's no way! Is that...

233
00:11:40,372 --> 00:11:41,706
...a Gatling gun?!

234
00:11:41,747 --> 00:11:42,915
[GROUP gasping]

235
00:11:42,957 --> 00:11:46,127
[JACK panting]

236
00:11:46,169 --> 00:11:48,254
[gasps]

237
00:11:48,296 --> 00:11:50,048
[JACK grunts]

238
00:11:51,174 --> 00:11:53,176
[JACK groans]

239
00:11:58,306 --> 00:12:00,684
[ARTERTON]
More!

240
00:12:03,645 --> 00:12:08,316
Don't stop firing! I want
him turned into Swiss cheese!

241
00:12:10,610 --> 00:12:13,112
[MORAN] It's no good.
Thing's built too sturdy.

242
00:12:13,154 --> 00:12:16,658
No way I can disable it.
I might get it to misfire

243
00:12:16,700 --> 00:12:19,452
if I could get a
bullet down that barrel.

244
00:12:19,494 --> 00:12:21,162
But the angle's
wrong from up here.

245
00:12:21,204 --> 00:12:23,039
[gasps] I have an idea!

246
00:12:23,081 --> 00:12:24,165
Follow me!

247
00:12:24,207 --> 00:12:25,917
[MORAN grunts]

248
00:12:27,544 --> 00:12:30,422
[JACK panting]

249
00:12:31,923 --> 00:12:33,299
[BONDE]

250
00:12:38,846 --> 00:12:40,098
[MORAN grunts]

251
00:12:40,139 --> 00:12:41,849
[MORAN]
How unorthodox,

252
00:12:41,891 --> 00:12:44,519
but then again,
that's your style.

253
00:12:45,562 --> 00:12:46,938
[MORAN]
Ready.

254
00:12:55,821 --> 00:12:57,031
Huh?

255
00:12:57,073 --> 00:12:58,658
[POLICE yell]

256
00:13:02,203 --> 00:13:03,580
Whew.

257
00:13:03,622 --> 00:13:05,164
[chuckles]

258
00:13:07,292 --> 00:13:09,835
[BOTH chuckle]

259
00:13:09,877 --> 00:13:12,547
[POLICE groaning, coughing]

260
00:13:19,053 --> 00:13:20,639
[MILVERTON]
I don't know what party's

261
00:13:20,680 --> 00:13:24,768
instigated this chaos,
but the tide has turned.

262
00:13:24,809 --> 00:13:26,144
It's bad!

263
00:13:26,185 --> 00:13:28,187
We didn't account
for a fake showing up!

264
00:13:28,229 --> 00:13:29,981
The entire plan's upside down!

265
00:13:30,022 --> 00:13:31,190
[MILVERTON]
Yes.

266
00:13:31,232 --> 00:13:34,569
This affair has left me
deeply troubled, as well.

267
00:13:34,611 --> 00:13:37,989
Far from what I expected
when I took the job.

268
00:13:38,030 --> 00:13:41,576
All that work building up the
mythological "Jack the Ripper"

269
00:13:41,618 --> 00:13:44,120
through the power of the media.

270
00:13:44,162 --> 00:13:46,080
[MILVERTON] And in a single
night.

271
00:13:46,122 --> 00:13:49,083
He has dissolved the conflict we
orchestrated between

272
00:13:49,125 --> 00:13:53,921
the Vigilance Committee and the
Yard.

273
00:13:53,963 --> 00:13:57,550
[JACK grunts, groans]

274
00:13:57,592 --> 00:14:00,094
[FRED]
Master.

275
00:14:00,136 --> 00:14:01,929
[JACK]
Fred, are you...?

276
00:14:01,971 --> 00:14:03,765
You'll want to head
on through that door.

277
00:14:03,807 --> 00:14:06,685
You can reach the
sewer from there.

278
00:14:06,726 --> 00:14:07,852
Leave the rest to me.

279
00:14:07,893 --> 00:14:11,105
[JACK]
Right. You're on now.

280
00:14:11,147 --> 00:14:14,442
[gasps] He's this way!
In the alley!

281
00:14:14,484 --> 00:14:15,527
[POLICEMAN 16C]
The monster's down here!

282
00:14:15,568 --> 00:14:17,278
[CIVILIAN 16F]
Hold it, Jack!

283
00:14:18,196 --> 00:14:21,907
[JACK sighs, groans]

284
00:14:22,742 --> 00:14:25,870
[JACK]
Ah, I may be getting old.

285
00:14:25,911 --> 00:14:30,792
But, still. I bought
you your hour, William.

286
00:14:30,834 --> 00:14:33,461
[MAN 16A grunts]
Confound it all!

287
00:14:33,503 --> 00:14:35,213
Our plan is ruined!

288
00:14:35,254 --> 00:14:36,589
The vigilantes and the Yard

289
00:14:36,631 --> 00:14:39,133
were just moments away from
going at each other's throats.

290
00:14:39,175 --> 00:14:40,552
Keep your head about you.

291
00:14:40,593 --> 00:14:41,803
Another dead prostitute

292
00:14:41,845 --> 00:14:43,971
will turn the situation
right back around.

293
00:14:44,013 --> 00:14:45,223
He's right.

294
00:14:45,264 --> 00:14:47,475
Nothing will save those
power-hungry elites from us.

295
00:14:47,517 --> 00:14:48,727
We'll send them
straight to hell!

296
00:14:48,768 --> 00:14:49,394
Quiet.

297
00:14:49,435 --> 00:14:50,978
[MAN 16A gasps]

298
00:14:52,438 --> 00:14:53,981
Oi, kill the lights!

299
00:14:54,023 --> 00:14:55,400
[MAN 16B blows]

300
00:14:58,152 --> 00:15:00,405
Hell, you say?

301
00:15:00,446 --> 00:15:02,907
It's been deserted...

302
00:15:02,948 --> 00:15:05,284
...and all of its devils...

303
00:15:06,411 --> 00:15:08,120
...are right here.

304
00:15:17,547 --> 00:15:20,007
[MAN 16D]
All right, who are you blokes?

305
00:15:20,049 --> 00:15:24,053
[WILLIAM]
James Moriarty, or perhaps

306
00:15:24,095 --> 00:15:27,973
it'll be simpler for you if
I just say the Lord of Crime.

307
00:15:28,015 --> 00:15:30,142
You're the Lord of Crime?

308
00:15:30,184 --> 00:15:33,438
[WILLIAM] And we are here
to deliver your punishment

309
00:15:33,479 --> 00:15:35,940
for your Jack the Ripper scheme.

310
00:15:35,981 --> 00:15:38,693
Those women's souls
cry out for vengeance.

311
00:15:38,735 --> 00:15:40,986
He really knows what's going on.

312
00:15:41,028 --> 00:15:42,363
[MAN 16C]
A moment.

313
00:15:42,405 --> 00:15:44,073
[footsteps]

314
00:15:44,115 --> 00:15:46,534
You are trying to plunge
this country into chaos.

315
00:15:46,576 --> 00:15:49,954
That is to say to start a
revolution--the same as us.

316
00:15:49,995 --> 00:15:52,791
You of all people must
understand our motives.

317
00:15:52,832 --> 00:15:55,042
At the expense of
a few useless dregs,

318
00:15:55,084 --> 00:15:56,335
we are on the
verge of delivering

319
00:15:56,377 --> 00:15:59,004
a stunning blow to this
sick, corrupt nation.

320
00:15:59,046 --> 00:16:01,549
Imagine, if we were
to work together,

321
00:16:01,591 --> 00:16:04,969
could we not make our
sublime vision a reality?

322
00:16:05,010 --> 00:16:08,180
[WILLIAM] Are you saying,
for the sake of revolution,

323
00:16:08,222 --> 00:16:10,558
you think nothing of
mercilessly preying on

324
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:12,477
those poor souls
weaker than you?

325
00:16:12,518 --> 00:16:13,978
As is our right, sir!

326
00:16:14,019 --> 00:16:16,522
The strong eat the weak
and this is no different!

327
00:16:16,564 --> 00:16:18,691
The law of the jungle is
eternal,

328
00:16:18,733 --> 00:16:21,694
and guides the natural world and
all its workings.

329
00:16:21,736 --> 00:16:24,071
[chuckles] Is that so?

330
00:16:24,113 --> 00:16:27,074
I am relieved to
hear you say that.

331
00:16:27,116 --> 00:16:29,911
Then by your own reasoning,

332
00:16:29,953 --> 00:16:32,664
you'll have no quarrel when we
mercilessly take your lives,

333
00:16:32,705 --> 00:16:36,000
since as you've stated,
the strong eat the weak.

334
00:16:36,041 --> 00:16:36,876
[BOTH gasp]

335
00:16:36,918 --> 00:16:38,210
Why, you!

336
00:16:38,252 --> 00:16:41,088
[MAN 16C]
If that's your response...

337
00:16:41,130 --> 00:16:42,715
Carve 'em up, boys!

338
00:16:42,757 --> 00:16:45,343
Louis, there's eight. Ready?

339
00:16:45,384 --> 00:16:48,930
Yes. We'll have eight corpses.

340
00:16:48,972 --> 00:16:51,056
[MAN 16A grunts]

341
00:16:51,098 --> 00:16:52,600
[MAN 16A groans]

342
00:16:54,101 --> 00:16:57,480
[MAN 16E yells]

343
00:16:57,522 --> 00:16:59,524
[BOTH chuckle]

344
00:16:59,565 --> 00:17:00,733
[MAN 16G yells]

345
00:17:01,818 --> 00:17:04,529
[MAN 16G groans]

346
00:17:04,570 --> 00:17:05,279
They're beasts!

347
00:17:05,321 --> 00:17:06,531
We'll be killed!

348
00:17:06,572 --> 00:17:09,325
Quick! Go around the back!
We'll escape on the boat!

349
00:17:09,367 --> 00:17:10,409
[MAN 16F]
Right!

350
00:17:13,997 --> 00:17:14,873
[WILLIAM grunts]

351
00:17:14,914 --> 00:17:18,459
[groans] All that
blood for nothing.

352
00:17:18,501 --> 00:17:20,879
As long as those
three chaps survive,

353
00:17:20,920 --> 00:17:26,467
the plan can take root
and start over! [cackles]

354
00:17:26,509 --> 00:17:27,635
[WILLIAM chuckles]

355
00:17:27,677 --> 00:17:30,013
[WILLIAM] And do you suppose
while you assembled

356
00:17:30,054 --> 00:17:32,097
we sat idly by?

357
00:17:32,139 --> 00:17:37,102
Wh-Whatcha mean?

358
00:17:37,144 --> 00:17:39,063
[WILLIAM]
Now,

359
00:17:39,104 --> 00:17:41,649
which do you think is faster?

360
00:17:41,691 --> 00:17:44,235
The speed of their heels,

361
00:17:44,276 --> 00:17:45,904
or a lit fuse?

362
00:17:45,945 --> 00:17:47,697
Care to bet?

363
00:17:51,158 --> 00:17:56,121
[MEN panting]

364
00:18:00,585 --> 00:18:02,628
I see the exit!

365
00:18:04,463 --> 00:18:07,050
Nearly there!
We're home free!

366
00:18:09,802 --> 00:18:11,721
[FRED grunts]

367
00:18:16,350 --> 00:18:17,435
Moran.

368
00:18:17,476 --> 00:18:21,146
Yeah, that was our signal.
The mission's over.

369
00:18:26,444 --> 00:18:28,821
[LOUIS]
All that remains are the bodies.

370
00:18:28,863 --> 00:18:30,990
You're sure you
want to leave them here?

371
00:18:31,032 --> 00:18:33,993
Yes, the Yard will arrive soon.

372
00:18:34,035 --> 00:18:37,455
And eventually Holmes will
inspect the scene as well.

373
00:18:37,496 --> 00:18:38,873
[WILLIAM]
Based on what I know,

374
00:18:38,915 --> 00:18:42,001
he is certain to figure out
the full story behind this case.

375
00:18:42,043 --> 00:18:45,088
When he does, I'd like to
learn what his reaction is.

376
00:18:45,129 --> 00:18:46,881
[LOUIS]
I assume by "reaction,"

377
00:18:46,923 --> 00:18:49,508
you mean when it comes
to an inconvenient truth,

378
00:18:49,550 --> 00:18:52,553
or a convenient lie,
which will he choose?

379
00:18:52,595 --> 00:18:54,430
[WILLIAM]
That is the question.

380
00:18:55,431 --> 00:18:56,766
[MILVERTON]
Is that--?

381
00:18:56,808 --> 00:19:01,395
If I recall correctly, his name
is William James Moriarty.

382
00:19:01,437 --> 00:19:03,898
Second son of
the Moriarty family

383
00:19:03,940 --> 00:19:06,525
and young mathematics prodigy.

384
00:19:06,567 --> 00:19:11,238
Interesting, so that is the
man with whom I am competing.

385
00:19:11,280 --> 00:19:14,617
I see. I must thoroughly
investigate him at once

386
00:19:14,659 --> 00:19:17,120
and add him to the list.

387
00:19:17,161 --> 00:19:19,080
After all,

388
00:19:19,122 --> 00:19:24,794
I, Charles Augustus Milverton,
am thorough in my work.

389
00:19:32,343 --> 00:19:35,262
How gruesome. While
determining the cause of death

390
00:19:35,304 --> 00:19:37,473
is difficult due
to the explosion.

391
00:19:37,515 --> 00:19:40,643
These stab wounds
indicate a professional.

392
00:19:40,685 --> 00:19:43,312
We've come to
the same conclusion.

393
00:19:43,354 --> 00:19:44,647
Well, you've been quiet.

394
00:19:44,689 --> 00:19:46,565
Have you seen
anything we've missed?

395
00:19:46,607 --> 00:19:49,193
Have you, Holmes?

396
00:19:49,234 --> 00:19:50,987
Sherlock?

397
00:19:53,948 --> 00:19:55,992
[HOLMES]
Yeah.

398
00:19:56,034 --> 00:19:59,745
All eight were likely
victims of Jack the Ripper.

399
00:19:59,787 --> 00:20:01,246
After stabbing them,

400
00:20:01,288 --> 00:20:04,750
he used the explosion
as a decoy to get away.

401
00:20:04,792 --> 00:20:06,836
Makes total sense. Right then,

402
00:20:06,878 --> 00:20:09,714
we'll cordon off the area
and hunt him down.

403
00:20:09,755 --> 00:20:11,549
Your insight is
appreciated, Holmes.

404
00:20:11,590 --> 00:20:12,758
[footsteps]

405
00:20:12,800 --> 00:20:14,969
[HOLMES]
Honestly,

406
00:20:15,011 --> 00:20:19,557
such a thing does exist
as an inopportune truth.

407
00:20:19,598 --> 00:20:22,309
The previous night's
events cooled tensions

408
00:20:22,351 --> 00:20:24,436
between the Yard and
the Vigilance Committee,

409
00:20:24,478 --> 00:20:27,857
as well as solving
the Ripper case.

410
00:20:27,899 --> 00:20:30,109
This kind of sleight of hand,

411
00:20:30,151 --> 00:20:33,237
only one person
could pull it off.

412
00:20:33,278 --> 00:20:36,532
The guy fancies himself
some kind of Robin Hood!

413
00:20:36,574 --> 00:20:41,245
What're you thinking,
Lord of Crime? This is madness!

414
00:20:41,286 --> 00:20:44,248
[WILLIAM] So, that's the
direction you've chosen, Holmes.

415
00:20:44,289 --> 00:20:47,085
Very well, but you must know,

416
00:20:47,126 --> 00:20:49,294
the Yard certainly won't
be content allowing Jack

417
00:20:49,336 --> 00:20:52,423
to remain at large, never.

418
00:20:52,464 --> 00:20:55,551
Meaning, their
next move will be...

419
00:20:55,593 --> 00:20:58,971
[ARTERTON grumbling]

420
00:22:36,235 --> 00:22:37,111
William!

421
00:22:37,153 --> 00:22:38,445
Yes?

422
00:22:38,487 --> 00:22:40,614
[MORAN] Don't play dumb with me!
I demand an explanation!

423
00:22:40,656 --> 00:22:44,576
[JACK] Again with the shouting?
What's wrong, Moran?

424
00:22:44,618 --> 00:22:46,912
[WILLIAM] You're looking quite
fashionable, Maestro,

425
00:22:46,954 --> 00:22:47,663
as always.

426
00:22:47,705 --> 00:22:49,290
[JACK]
Of course, Young Will.

427
00:22:49,332 --> 00:22:52,251
This is my main line
of work at the moment.

428
00:22:52,293 --> 00:22:55,129
We wanted this to be
a surprise for you.

429
00:22:55,171 --> 00:22:58,423
I'd say it worked.
The maestro is our new butler.

430
00:22:58,465 --> 00:22:59,758
[MORAN]
Huh?!

431
00:22:59,800 --> 00:23:00,843
The thought of Louis

432
00:23:00,885 --> 00:23:03,179
keeping house for
two residences by himself.

433
00:23:03,221 --> 00:23:06,390
Well, I couldn't bear it.
It's better this way.

434
00:23:06,431 --> 00:23:09,476
He'll be able to take a
more active role in our plan.

435
00:23:09,518 --> 00:23:12,813
Yes. Thank you,
Brother. How thoughtful.

436
00:23:12,855 --> 00:23:14,106
[MORAN]
Thoughtful?!

437
00:23:14,148 --> 00:23:17,484
[JACK] Truly, I look forward to
working alongside you.

438
00:23:17,526 --> 00:23:20,279
[BONDE] What's the matter,
Moran? You look a little pale.

439
00:23:20,321 --> 00:23:23,908
[MORAN]
Are you kidding me?!

440
00:23:32,791 --> 00:23:35,211
[HERDER] Next time
on Moriarty the Patriot:

441
00:23:35,253 --> 00:23:37,713
"The Riot in New Scotland Yard."
